# Rule - Incremental Delivery

Finish one sprint backlog item (SBI) before starting the next. An SBI is finished when [`dod.mdc`](./dod.mdc) passes for it.

## Behavior

- Work on the current SBI named in `status.md`. Open `status.md` through `{workspace}/artifacts-map.md`.
- Do not start another SBI while the current one is not Done.
- When the current SBI depends on another item, do only the part that unblocks the current SBI.
- When a blocker stops the current SBI, tell the user what blocks it and wait for a decision before moving on.
- A new requirement found during the work becomes a new backlog item after the user confirms it. It is not added to the current SBI.

## Granularity

- The unit of delivery is one SBI, not a feature or an epic.
- Do not bundle two SBIs into one implementation pass.
